markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Using AI Tools

#### AI tools can support many aspects of teaching practice. They can save time and generate ideas, but they are most effective when used thoughtfully and with a clear purpose.

#### A helpful way to approach AI use is to pause and **THINK** before using it:

<div style="width:80%; max-width:900px; margin:0 auto; font-family:ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial; color:#292F36;">

<div style="border:1px solid #D9DDE3; border-radius:16px; overflow:hidden; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">

<!-- ROW -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr; border-bottom:1px solid #E8ECF0;">
<div style="background:#8C52BA; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:800; font-size:28px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">
T
</div>
<div style="padding:16px;">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:18px; margin-bottom:6px;">Task & Purpose</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
Start by being clear about why you are using AI. What task are you trying to support, and how will this improve your teaching? AI can be useful for generating drafts, ideas, or variations, but it should support your thinking—not replace it. If a tool is only making a task faster without improving the outcome, it may not be the right use.
</div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- ROW -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr; border-bottom:1px solid #E8ECF0;">
<div style="background:#8C52BA; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:800; font-size:28px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">
H
</div>
<div style="padding:16px;">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:18px; margin-bottom:6px;">Human Oversight</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
AI does not understand your students, your classroom context, or your instructional goals. Its outputs may sound polished but can be incomplete, inaccurate, or misaligned. Before using anything it produces, review and revise it carefully. Adapt it so it reflects your goals, your students’ needs, and your professional judgment.
</div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- ROW -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr; border-bottom:1px solid #E8ECF0;">
<div style="background:#8C52BA; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:800; font-size:28px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">
I
</div>
<div style="padding:16px;">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:18px; margin-bottom:6px;">Instructional Quality</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
Keep quality at the center of your decisions. Ask yourself whether the AI-generated material is accurate, aligned to standards, and appropriate for the level of rigor you expect. AI can help generate content quickly, but it cannot ensure that the content meets your expectations without your input.
</div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- ROW -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr; border-bottom:1px solid #E8ECF0;">
<div style="background:#8C52BA; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:800; font-size:28px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">
N
</div>
<div style="padding:16px;">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:18px; margin-bottom:6px;">No Sensitive Data</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
Protecting student privacy must remain a priority. Avoid entering personal or sensitive information about students, families, or colleagues into AI tools, and treat anything you input as potentially public. Be sure to follow your school or district’s policies and use only approved tools when applicable.
</div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- ROW -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr;">
<div style="background:#8C52BA; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:800; font-size:28px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">
K
</div>
<div style="padding:16px;">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:18px; margin-bottom:6px;">Keep Professional Judgment First</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
AI is a tool to support your work—not replace your expertise. Your knowledge of your students, your content, and your instructional goals should guide every decision. If something generated by AI doesn’t feel right, trust your judgment and adjust or discard it.
</div>
</div>
</div>

</div>
</div>

#### The THINK framework is a good starting point to evaluating when and how to use AI. We'll cover more around data privacy and other concerns around using AI in Module 5, Ensuring a Responsible Approach.
MARKDOWN
